WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.501
Some signs of progress

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.504
after a devastating three way train crash

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.573
rocked India over the weekend.

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.341
Crews have now cleared the rails,

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.110
allowing other trains to pass

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.611
through the crash site.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:12.812
It is one of the deadliest

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.147
India has ever seen.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.715
Nearly 300 people were killed,

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:17.684
more than a thousand injured.

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.485
We want to take you now

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:19.352
live to the scene

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:19.986
in Eastern

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:20.854
India with CNN's

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.856
Ivan Watson, who's there for us.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:23.423
Ivan,

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.491
how exactly does

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.427
something like this happen?

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.864
The authorities are saying

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:31.765
this was some kind of a

00:00:31.765 --> 00:00:33.700
switching malfunction.

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.469
That result resulted.

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.506
Boris in this kind of perfect storm

00:00:39.506 --> 00:00:41.041
of a train crash

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.077
with a staggering loss of lives.

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.312
The trains have started running again

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.080
through this area.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:48.782
Because the work crews have been working

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.183
feverishly there.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:53.920
But dozens of victims, their bodies

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.522
have yet to be identified.

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:02.128
Working on the railroad

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:04.764
an army of laborers

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.167
laying new rail by hand,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.837
racing to reopen this transport route

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.305
after one of the deadliest

00:01:12.305 --> 00:01:13.339
train disasters

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.809
India has seen in its modern history.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.312
On Friday night, three trains

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:21.948
collided in this area and everywhere

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.383
on the side of the tracks.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.652
In this rural part of eastern India,

00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:28.655
there are massive railroad cars

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:30.690
that were well,

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:31.524
as you can see,

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.860
severely damaged in this collision.

00:01:34.194 --> 00:01:37.263
This vehicle here, this car was reserved

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:38.998
for people with disabilities.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:40.533
You can still see people's

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.302
personal belongings

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:45.705
down below, right outside.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.507
It began with a passenger train

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:51.211
moving at 128 kilometers or 80 miles

00:01:51.211 --> 00:01:52.245
per hour,

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:54.614
slamming into a parked freight train

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:58.084
colliding after dark in this rural area.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:02:00.086
Villagers rescued passengers.

